From 37ef9979c523e3c287c136e625d5a0f78bb5d6ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 21:47:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Squares & Cubes Explorer as app 04
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Vendors drstockinvesting/exploration_perfect_squares_and_cubes into
apps/squares-cubes/ and gives it a page, following the process in the
README's "Adding an app".

The one transformation the vendor script performs is lifting the app's
inline <style> into styles.css. Upstream is deliberately a single
double-clickable file, but apply-site-chrome.js injects the @font-face
blocks by rewriting a payload stylesheet and only looks for
apps/<slug>/styles.css or style.css — a single-file app hits the
`continue` and is skipped silently. Vendored whole, it would keep
whatever base64 it arrived with and be the one app that quietly stops
following when the site's fonts change. The split puts its fonts back
under the generator's ownership. The app reads no styles back from the
DOM, so the split is behaviour-neutral.

Category colour is --tc, the last unused accent, and already the app's
own squares colour — so the card and the figures agree without a second
decision. No localStorage keys and no third-party code.

The a11y notes are marked keyboard: 'partial'. Everything the app
teaches is keyboard-reachable — the slider takes arrow keys, S/C/E/R/D
drive the modes, and a live region announces the side length, total and
notation on every change — but rotating the cube is a drag with no
keyboard equivalent, and the figures themselves are decorative to a
screen reader.

Verified: apply-site-chrome.js runs clean and is idempotent (second run
produces no diff), check-external.js reports zero external origins across
41 files, and the page renders from file:// with the app booting inside
the frame in Nunito and Space Mono, driven through both modes, with no
console errors and no non-file:// requests.

Note for whoever runs it next: build-og-cards.js could not run in the
authoring container (it probes fixed Chrome paths and the container runs
as root, which modern Chromium refuses without --no-sandbox).
assets/og-squares-cubes.png was rendered separately at the same
1200x630 spec; the other four cards are untouched. The script itself is
unmodified and will work as documented on a normal machine.

